# Environment files
# The BARE `.env` too: it holds real secrets (AUTH_SECRET, DB credentials) and
# the build context is the repository root, so any `COPY . .` would bake it into
# an image layer. Only the `.local`/`.development.local` variants were ignored
# before, which left the actual `.env` readable inside every built image.
#
# ── THE `**/` VARIANTS ARE NOT REDUNDANT ────────────────────────────────────
# An unqualified pattern only anchors at the CONTEXT ROOT. `.env.*` therefore
# never matched `apps/web/.env.local`, and the dependency-builder image shipped
# that file — with a real `AUTH_SECRET` in it — into a layer. Measured:
# `ls /app/apps/web/.env.local` inside the built image succeeded, and Turbo's
# `globalCacheInputs.files` listed it as a global-dependency input.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# IDE files
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Git
# `.gitignore` is NOT ignored: the dependency-builder image builds a repository from it so
# Turbo skips the same untracked files git does.
.git
.github

# Build leftovers: per-process temp files / caches that differ on every run
**/.pkg-build-types.*
**/.eslintcache

# Docker
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml

# Testing
coverage
.nyc_output
**/__tests__
vitest.config.*

# Docs & examples (not needed for production images)
docs
README.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Developer tooling / experiments (exclude from prod context)
_experiment
bun-preload-script
test-url.js

# Logs
# Log FILES only. A bare `logs` entry used to sit here and it matches ANY path
# component named `logs` — including real route directories such as
# apps/web/src/app/dashboard/**/logs/ and .../docker/logs/. Those pages were
# therefore excluded from the build context AND from `docker compose watch`
# sync, so edits to them silently never reached the dev container.
*.log

# Cache directories
.cache
.parcel-cache

# Temporary files
.tmp
.temp

# Project specific
analyze/